{"toolCallId":"call_56c49445869446c981f9d0d348fd256f","title":"Edit file","kind":"edit","content":[{"type":"diff","path":"/private/tmp/claude-501/-Users-michelkerkmeester-MEGA-Development-Code-Environment-Public/fcd93cd7-b3f2-45e6-b976-87fabe792df3/scratchpad/speed-loop/w8a66e200e3/tree/specs/zz-bench-authoring/001-completeness-min-percent/tasks.md","oldText":"---\ntitle: \"Tasks: Add a min-percent option to calculate-completeness.sh\"\ndescription: \"Task Format: T### [P?] Description (file path)\"\ntrigger_phrases:\n  - \"completeness min percent tasks\"\nimportance_tier: \"normal\"\ncontextType: \"general\"\n---\n<!-- SPECKIT_TEMPLATE_SOURCE: tasks-core | v2.3 -->\n# Tasks: Add a min-percent option to calculate-completeness.sh\n\n<!-- SPECKIT_LEVEL: 1 -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:notation -->\n## Task Notation\n\n| Prefix | Meaning |\n|--------|---------|\n| `[ ]` | Pending |\n| `[x]` | Completed |\n| `[P]` | Parallelizable |\n| `[B]` | Blocked |\n\n**Task Format**: `T### [P?] Description (file path). Verify: <command> prints <expected output>`\n\n**Variables**: `S` is `.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/spec/calculate-completeness.sh`. `T` is a temp fixture folder whose report prints `Overall Completion: 0%`.\n<!-- /ANCHOR:notation -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:phase-1 -->\n## Phase 1: Setup\n\n- [ ] T001 Read the option loop, the tail and the exit-code comment in `S`, and record the current exit codes. Verify: `rg -n 'exit [0-9]' \"$S\"` prints the existing `exit 0` plus the error exits.\n- [ ] T002 Build the fixture: `T=$(mktemp -d); printf '[%s]\\n' TBD > \"$T/spec.md\"`. Verify: `bash \"$S\" \"$T\"` prints `Overall Completion: 0%`.\n- [ ] T003 [P] Capture the baseline report for later diffing: `bash \"$S\" \"$T\" > baseline.txt`. Verify: the command exits 0 and `wc -l < baseline.txt` prints a non-zero count.\n<!-- /ANCHOR:phase-1 -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:phase-2 -->\n## Phase 2: Implementation\n\n- [ ] T004 Add a `MIN_PERCENT` global and a `--min-percent` case to the option loop that validates `^[0-9]+$` and a value from 0 to 100, exiting 1 with a stderr usage error otherwise (`S`). Verify: `bash \"$S\" --min-percent abc \"$T\"` exits 1 and `bash \"$S\" --min-percent 90 \"$T\"` is accepted.\n- [ ] T005 Replace the unconditional `exit 0` with the threshold comparison, using `OVERALL_PERCENTAGE` in folder mode and the single-file percentage under `--file`, so a completion below `MIN_PERCENT` exits 3 and anything else exits 0 (`S`). Verify: `bash \"$S\" --min-percent 90 \"$T\"` exits 3 and `bash \"$S\" --min-percent 0 \"$T\"` exits 0.\n- [ ] T006 Add the `--min-percent <N>` line to `show_help` and list exit 3 in the trailing exit-code comment (`S`). Verify: `bash \"$S\" --help` prints one `--min-percent` line and `rg -n '3 - ' \"$S\"` prints the below-threshold entry.\n- [ ] T007 [P] Confirm the option appears only where intended (`S`). Verify: `rg -n 'min-percent|MIN_PERCENT' \"$S\"` lists hits only in `show_help`, the option loop and the tail, with none inside `output_text` or `output_json`.\n<!-- /ANCHOR:phase-2 -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:phase-3 -->\n## Phase 3: Verification\n\n- [ ] T008 Run the exit matrix on the fixture. Verify: no option exits 0, `--min-percent 0` exits 0, `--min-percent 1` exits 3 and `--min-percent 90` exits 3.\n- [ ] T009 Diff the text report with and without the option. Verify: `diff <(bash \"$S\" \"$T\" || true) <(bash \"$S\" --min-percent 90 \"$T\" || true)` prints nothing.\n- [ ] T010 [P] Diff the JSON report with and without the option. Verify: `diff <(bash \"$S\" --json \"$T\" || true) <(bash \"$S\" --json --min-percent 90 \"$T\" || true)` prints nothing.\n- [ ] T011 Run the matrix on a complete fixture: `C=$(mktemp -d); printf '## 1. METADATA\\nFilled content.\\n' > \"$C/spec.md\"`. Verify: `bash \"$S\" --min-percent 100 \"$C\"` exits 0 and `bash \"$S\" --min-percent 101 \"$C\"` exits 1 with a stderr message.\n- [ ] T012 Run spec validation on this packet as a regression check. Verify: `bash .skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/spec/validate.sh specs/zz-bench-authoring/001-completeness-min-percent --strict` prints `RESULT: PASSED`.\n<!-- /ANCHOR:phase-3 -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:completion -->\n## Completion Criteria\n\n- [ ] All tasks marked `[x]`\n- [ ] No `[B]` blocked tasks remaining\n- [ ] Manual verification passed\n- [ ] Exit matrix and both output diffs recorded in `implementation-summary.md`\n<!-- /ANCHOR:completion -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:cross-refs -->\n## Cross-References\n\n- **Specification**: See `spec.md`\n- **Plan**: See `plan.md`\n<!-- /ANCHOR:cross-refs -->\n\n---\n","newText":"---\ntitle: \"Tasks: Add a min-percent option to calculate-completeness.sh\"\ndescription: \"Task Format: T### [P?] Description (file path)\"\ntrigger_phrases:\n  - \"completeness min percent tasks\"\nimportance_tier: \"normal\"\ncontextType: \"general\"\n---\n<!-- SPECKIT_TEMPLATE_SOURCE: tasks-core | v2.3 -->\n# Tasks: Add a min-percent option to calculate-completeness.sh\n\n<!-- SPECKIT_LEVEL: 1 -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:notation -->\n## Task Notation\n\n| Prefix | Meaning |\n|--------|---------|\n| `[ ]` | Pending |\n| `[x]` | Completed |\n| `[P]` | Parallelizable |\n| `[B]` | Blocked |\n\n**Task Format**: `T### [P?] Description (file path). Verify: <command> prints <expected output>`\n\n**Variables**: `S` is `.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/spec/calculate-completeness.sh`. `T` is a temp fixture folder whose report prints `Overall Completion: 0%`.\n<!-- /ANCHOR:notation -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:phase-1 -->\n## Phase 1: Setup\n\n- [ ] T001 Read the option loop, the tail and the exit-code comment in `S`, and record the current exit codes. Verify: `rg -n 'exit [0-9]' \"$S\"` prints the existing `exit 0` plus the error exits.\n- [ ] T002 Build the fixture: `T=$(mktemp -d); printf '[%s]\\n' TBD > \"$T/spec.md\"`. Verify: `bash \"$S\" \"$T\"` prints `Overall Completion: 0%`.\n- [ ] T003 [P] Capture the baseline report for later diffing: `bash \"$S\" \"$T\" > baseline.txt`. Verify: the command exits 0 and `wc -l < baseline.txt` prints a non-zero count.\n<!-- /ANCHOR:phase-1 -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:phase-2 -->\n## Phase 2: Implementation\n\n- [ ] T004 Add a `MIN_PERCENT` global and a `--min-percent` case to the option loop that validates `^[0-9]+$` and a value from 0 to 100, exiting 1 with a stderr usage error otherwise (`S`). Verify: `bash \"$S\" --min-percent abc \"$T\"` exits 1 and `bash \"$S\" --min-percent 90 \"$T\"` is accepted.\n- [ ] T005 Replace the unconditional `exit 0` with the threshold comparison, using `OVERALL_PERCENTAGE` in folder mode and the single-file percentage under `--file`, so a completion below `MIN_PERCENT` exits 3 and anything else exits 0 (`S`). Verify: `bash \"$S\" --min-percent 90 \"$T\"` exits 3 and `bash \"$S\" --min-percent 0 \"$T\"` exits 0.\n- [ ] T006 Add the `--min-percent <N>` line to `show_help` and list exit 3 in the trailing exit-code comment (`S`). Verify: `bash \"$S\" --help` prints one `--min-percent` line and `rg -n '3 - ' \"$S\"` prints the below-threshold entry.\n- [ ] T007 [P] Confirm the option appears only where intended (`S`). Verify: `rg -n 'min-percent|MIN_PERCENT' \"$S\"` lists hits only in `show_help`, the option loop and the tail, with none inside `output_text` or `output_json`.\n- [ ] T013 Implement REQ-007: emit a boolean `min_percent_met` in the `--json` output when `--json` and `--min-percent` are both passed, true when the reported Overall Completion is at or above `MIN_PERCENT` and false otherwise, leaving the JSON unchanged when the option is absent (`S`). Verify: `bash \"$S\" --json --min-percent 90 \"$T\"` prints `\"min_percent_met\": false`, `bash \"$S\" --json --min-percent 0 \"$T\"` prints `\"min_percent_met\": true`, and `bash \"$S\" --json \"$T\"` prints no `min_percent_met` key.\n<!-- /ANCHOR:phase-2 -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:phase-3 -->\n## Phase 3: Verification\n\n- [ ] T008 Run the exit matrix on the fixture. Verify: no option exits 0, `--min-percent 0` exits 0, `--min-percent 1` exits 3 and `--min-percent 90` exits 3.\n- [ ] T009 Diff the text report with and without the option. Verify: `diff <(bash \"$S\" \"$T\" || true) <(bash \"$S\" --min-percent 90 \"$T\" || true)` prints nothing.\n- [ ] T010 [P] Diff the JSON report with and without the option. Verify: `diff <(bash \"$S\" --json \"$T\" || true) <(bash \"$S\" --json --min-percent 90 \"$T\" || true)` prints nothing.\n- [ ] T011 Run the matrix on a complete fixture: `C=$(mktemp -d); printf '## 1. METADATA\\nFilled content.\\n' > \"$C/spec.md\"`. Verify: `bash \"$S\" --min-percent 100 \"$C\"` exits 0 and `bash \"$S\" --min-percent 101 \"$C\"` exits 1 with a stderr message.\n- [ ] T012 Run spec validation on this packet as a regression check. Verify: `bash .skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/spec/validate.sh specs/zz-bench-authoring/001-completeness-min-percent --strict` prints `RESULT: PASSED`.\n<!-- /ANCHOR:phase-3 -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:completion -->\n## Completion Criteria\n\n- [ ] All tasks marked `[x]`\n- [ ] No `[B]` blocked tasks remaining\n- [ ] Manual verification passed\n- [ ] Exit matrix and both output diffs recorded in `implementation-summary.md`\n<!-- /ANCHOR:completion -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:cross-refs -->\n## Cross-References\n\n- **Specification**: See `spec.md`\n- **Plan**: See `plan.md`\n<!-- /ANCHOR:cross-refs -->\n\n---\n","_meta":{"cognition.ai/linesAdded":1,"cognition.ai/linesRemoved":0}}],"locations":[{"path":"/private/tmp/claude-501/-Users-michelkerkmeester-MEGA-Development-Code-Environment-Public/fcd93cd7-b3f2-45e6-b976-87fabe792df3/scratchpad/speed-loop/w8a66e200e3/tree/specs/zz-bench-authoring/001-completeness-min-percent/tasks.md"}],"rawInput":{"file_path":"/private/tmp/claude-501/-Users-michelkerkmeester-MEGA-Development-Code-Environment-Public/fcd93cd7-b3f2-45e6-b976-87fabe792df3/scratchpad/speed-loop/w8a66e200e3/tree/specs/zz-bench-authoring/001-completeness-min-percent/tasks.md"},"_meta":{"cognition.ai/inferenceToolName":"edit"}}
{"toolCallId":"call_891c59080ae147d5aa5e768d930c9d52","title":"Ran node, echo","kind":"execute","content":[{"type":"content","content":{"type":"resource","resource":{"mimeType":"text/x-shellscript","text":"node .skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/spec/repair-derived.cjs --folder specs/zz-bench-authoring/001-completeness-min-percent --apply; echo \"EXIT_STATUS=$?\"","uri":"tool://preview"},"_meta":{"cognition.ai/preview_is_shell_command":true}}}],"rawInput":{"command":"node .skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/spec/repair-derived.cjs --folder specs/zz-bench-authoring/001-completeness-min-percent --apply; echo \"EXIT_STATUS=$?\"","workdir":"/private/tmp/claude-501/-Users-michelkerkmeester-MEGA-Development-Code-Environment-Public/fcd93cd7-b3f2-45e6-b976-87fabe792df3/scratchpad/speed-loop/w8a66e200e3/tree"},"_meta":{"cognition.ai/commandNames":["node","echo"],"cognition.ai/inferenceToolName":"exec"}}
{"toolCallId":"call_ce20901e1afc4ee7891b8d03c2b65753","title":"Edit file","kind":"edit","content":[{"type":"diff","path":"/private/tmp/claude-501/-Users-michelkerkmeester-MEGA-Development-Code-Environment-Public/fcd93cd7-b3f2-45e6-b976-87fabe792df3/scratchpad/speed-loop/w8a66e200e3/tree/specs/zz-bench-authoring/001-completeness-min-percent/spec.md","oldText":"---\ntitle: \"Feature Specification: Add a min-percent option to calculate-completeness.sh\"\ndescription: \"Add a --min-percent <N> option to calculate-completeness.sh so a caller can fail a check on an incomplete packet, exiting 3 when the reported completion is below N and 0 otherwise while leaving the report output unchanged.\"\ntrigger_phrases:\n  - \"completeness min percent\"\n  - \"add a min percent option to calculate completeness\"\nimportance_tier: \"normal\"\ncontextType: \"general\"\n---\n<!-- SPECKIT_TEMPLATE_SOURCE: spec-core | v2.3 -->\n# Feature Specification: Add a min-percent option to calculate-completeness.sh\n\n<!-- SPECKIT_LEVEL: 1 -->\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:metadata -->\n## 1. METADATA\n\n| Field | Value |\n|-------|-------|\n| **Level** | 1 |\n| **Priority** | P1 |\n| **Status** | Draft |\n| **Created** | 2026-10-26 |\n| **Branch** | `scaffold/001-completeness-min-percent` |\n<!-- /ANCHOR:metadata -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:problem -->\n## 2. PROBLEM & PURPOSE\n\n### Problem Statement\n`calculate-completeness.sh` prints a completion report and then always exits 0, so a caller cannot tell an incomplete packet from a complete one without parsing stdout. Every wrapper that greps the `Overall Completion:` line couples itself to the human-readable report and breaks when that formatting changes.\n\n### Purpose\nAdd `--min-percent <N>` so a caller can make an incomplete packet fail the call by exit status, without changing the report a human reads.\n<!-- /ANCHOR:problem -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:scope -->\n## 3. SCOPE\n\n### In Scope\n- Add `--min-percent <N>` parsing to the argument loop, storing N for the final exit decision.\n- Exit 3 when the reported completion is below N and 0 when it is at or above N.\n- Keep stdout and stderr byte-identical with and without the option, in text and JSON modes.\n- Document the option in `--help` and in the trailing exit-code comment block.\n- Reject a missing, non-integer or out-of-range N with exit 1 and a stderr message.\n\n### Out of Scope\n- Changing how completion is calculated - the placeholder patterns and percentage formula stay as they are.\n- Adding a config file or environment variable for the threshold - callers already pass flags, and a flag keeps the threshold per-invocation.\n- Gating other spec-kit scripts - each script owns its own exit codes.\n- Turning `--quality` warnings into failures - that mode stays advisory.\n\n### Files to Change\n\n| File Path | Change Type | Description |\n|-----------|-------------|-------------|\n| `.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/spec/calculate-completeness.sh` | Modify | Parse `--min-percent <N>`, compare it with the reported completion, and set exit 3 on a shortfall; update `show_help` and the exit-code comment block. |\n<!-- /ANCHOR:scope -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:requirements -->\n## 4. REQUIREMENTS\n\n### P0 - Blockers (MUST complete)\n\n| ID | Requirement | Acceptance Criteria |\n|----|-------------|---------------------|\n| REQ-001 | Accept `--min-percent <N>` in the argument loop without consuming the spec folder or `--file` path | `calculate-completeness.sh --min-percent 90 specs/<folder>` analyzes the named folder and prints the normal report |\n| REQ-002 | Exit 3 when the reported completion is below N | On a fixture whose Overall Completion is 0%, `--min-percent 90` exits 3 |\n| REQ-003 | Exit 0 when the reported completion is at or above N | On the same fixture, `--min-percent 0` exits 0; the boundary value equal to the completion also exits 0 |\n| REQ-004 | Leave the report output unchanged whether or not the option is present | `diff` of stdout from the two invocations is empty in text mode and in `--json` mode |\n\n### P1 - Required (complete OR user-approved deferral)\n\n| ID | Requirement | Acceptance Criteria |\n|----|-------------|---------------------|\n| REQ-005 | Reject a missing, non-integer or out-of-range N with exit 1 and a stderr error, leaving stdout empty | `--min-percent` with no value, `--min-percent abc` and `--min-percent 101` each exit 1 and print a usage error to stderr |\n| REQ-006 | Document the option in `--help` and in the trailing exit-code comment block | `--help` lists `--min-percent <N>` once, and the comment block lists exit 3 as a below-threshold result |\n<!-- /ANCHOR:requirements -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:success-criteria -->\n## 5. SUCCESS CRITERIA\n\n- **SC-001**: `calculate-completeness.sh --min-percent 90 <fixture>` exits 3 on a 0% fixture, and `--min-percent 0 <fixture>` exits 0.\n- **SC-002**: stdout from `<script> <folder>` and `<script> --min-percent 90 <folder>` is byte-identical in text mode and in `--json` mode.\n- **SC-003**: Without the option the script still exits 0 on the same fixture, so existing callers keep working.\n- **SC-004**: `--min-percent 101` exits 1, writes one usage error to stderr and writes nothing to stdout.\n<!-- /ANCHOR:success-criteria -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:risks -->\n## 6. RISKS & DEPENDENCIES\n\n| Type | Item | Impact | Mitigation |\n|------|------|--------|------------|\n| Dependency | `bc` and Bash 3.2 integer arithmetic, both already used by the script | The comparison cannot run if `bc` is missing | Reuse the integer the report already prints; the script's existing `bc` guard keeps its current error path |\n| Risk | A caller treats exit 3 as a script error and aborts a pipeline that used to continue | Med | Document exit 3 in `--help` and the exit-code comment, and keep exit 1 reserved for real errors |\n| Risk | A value with leading zeros or a sign compares as a string rather than a number | Low | Validate N against `^[0-9]+$` and normalize it to a base-10 integer before the comparison |\n<!-- /ANCHOR:risks -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:questions -->\n## 7. OPEN QUESTIONS\n\n- Does `--min-percent` also apply under `--file`? Decision: yes - it compares against that file's reported completion, so the gate behaves the same in both modes.\n- Is N inclusive? Decision: yes - a completion equal to N passes, matching the request's \"below N\".\n- Does the option change stderr? Decision: no - stderr is unchanged, so existing warning consumers keep working.\n<!-- /ANCHOR:questions -->\n\n---\n","newText":"---\ntitle: \"Feature Specification: Add a min-percent option to calculate-completeness.sh\"\ndescription: \"Add a --min-percent <N> option to calculate-completeness.sh so a caller can fail a check on an incomplete packet, exiting 3 when the reported completion is below N and 0 otherwise while leaving the report output unchanged.\"\ntrigger_phrases:\n  - \"completeness min percent\"\n  - \"add a min percent option to calculate completeness\"\nimportance_tier: \"normal\"\ncontextType: \"general\"\n---\n<!-- SPECKIT_TEMPLATE_SOURCE: spec-core | v2.3 -->\n# Feature Specification: Add a min-percent option to calculate-completeness.sh\n\n<!-- SPECKIT_LEVEL: 1 -->\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:metadata -->\n## 1. METADATA\n\n| Field | Value |\n|-------|-------|\n| **Level** | 1 |\n| **Priority** | P1 |\n| **Status** | Draft |\n| **Created** | 2026-10-26 |\n| **Branch** | `scaffold/001-completeness-min-percent` |\n<!-- /ANCHOR:metadata -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:problem -->\n## 2. PROBLEM & PURPOSE\n\n### Problem Statement\n`calculate-completeness.sh` prints a completion report and then always exits 0, so a caller cannot tell an incomplete packet from a complete one without parsing stdout. Every wrapper that greps the `Overall Completion:` line couples itself to the human-readable report and breaks when that formatting changes.\n\n### Purpose\nAdd `--min-percent <N>` so a caller can make an incomplete packet fail the call by exit status, without changing the report a human reads.\n<!-- /ANCHOR:problem -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:scope -->\n## 3. SCOPE\n\n### In Scope\n- Add `--min-percent <N>` parsing to the argument loop, storing N for the final exit decision.\n- Exit 3 when the reported completion is below N and 0 when it is at or above N.\n- Keep stdout and stderr byte-identical with and without the option, in text and JSON modes.\n- Document the option in `--help` and in the trailing exit-code comment block.\n- Reject a missing, non-integer or out-of-range N with exit 1 and a stderr message.\n\n### Out of Scope\n- Changing how completion is calculated - the placeholder patterns and percentage formula stay as they are.\n- Adding a config file or environment variable for the threshold - callers already pass flags, and a flag keeps the threshold per-invocation.\n- Gating other spec-kit scripts - each script owns its own exit codes.\n- Turning `--quality` warnings into failures - that mode stays advisory.\n\n### Files to Change\n\n| File Path | Change Type | Description |\n|-----------|-------------|-------------|\n| `.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/spec/calculate-completeness.sh` | Modify | Parse `--min-percent <N>`, compare it with the reported completion, and set exit 3 on a shortfall; update `show_help` and the exit-code comment block. |\n<!-- /ANCHOR:scope -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:requirements -->\n## 4. REQUIREMENTS\n\n### P0 - Blockers (MUST complete)\n\n| ID | Requirement | Acceptance Criteria |\n|----|-------------|---------------------|\n| REQ-001 | Accept `--min-percent <N>` in the argument loop without consuming the spec folder or `--file` path | `calculate-completeness.sh --min-percent 90 specs/<folder>` analyzes the named folder and prints the normal report |\n| REQ-002 | Exit 3 when the reported completion is below N | On a fixture whose Overall Completion is 0%, `--min-percent 90` exits 3 |\n| REQ-003 | Exit 0 when the reported completion is at or above N | On the same fixture, `--min-percent 0` exits 0; the boundary value equal to the completion also exits 0 |\n| REQ-004 | Leave the report output unchanged whether or not the option is present | `diff` of stdout from the two invocations is empty in text mode and in `--json` mode |\n\n### P1 - Required (complete OR user-approved deferral)\n\n| ID | Requirement | Acceptance Criteria |\n|----|-------------|---------------------|\n| REQ-005 | Reject a missing, non-integer or out-of-range N with exit 1 and a stderr error, leaving stdout empty | `--min-percent` with no value, `--min-percent abc` and `--min-percent 101` each exit 1 and print a usage error to stderr |\n| REQ-006 | Document the option in `--help` and in the trailing exit-code comment block | `--help` lists `--min-percent <N>` once, and the comment block lists exit 3 as a below-threshold result |\n| REQ-007 | Add a boolean `min_percent_met` field to the `--json` output when `--json` and `--min-percent` are passed together, true when Overall Completion is at or above N and false otherwise | `calculate-completeness.sh --json --min-percent 90 <0% fixture>` prints `\"min_percent_met\": false` and `--json --min-percent 0` prints `\"min_percent_met\": true` |\n<!-- /ANCHOR:requirements -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:success-criteria -->\n## 5. SUCCESS CRITERIA\n\n- **SC-001**: `calculate-completeness.sh --min-percent 90 <fixture>` exits 3 on a 0% fixture, and `--min-percent 0 <fixture>` exits 0.\n- **SC-002**: stdout from `<script> <folder>` and `<script> --min-percent 90 <folder>` is byte-identical in text mode and in `--json` mode.\n- **SC-003**: Without the option the script still exits 0 on the same fixture, so existing callers keep working.\n- **SC-004**: `--min-percent 101` exits 1, writes one usage error to stderr and writes nothing to stdout.\n<!-- /ANCHOR:success-criteria -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:risks -->\n## 6. RISKS & DEPENDENCIES\n\n| Type | Item | Impact | Mitigation |\n|------|------|--------|------------|\n| Dependency | `bc` and Bash 3.2 integer arithmetic, both already used by the script | The comparison cannot run if `bc` is missing | Reuse the integer the report already prints; the script's existing `bc` guard keeps its current error path |\n| Risk | A caller treats exit 3 as a script error and aborts a pipeline that used to continue | Med | Document exit 3 in `--help` and the exit-code comment, and keep exit 1 reserved for real errors |\n| Risk | A value with leading zeros or a sign compares as a string rather than a number | Low | Validate N against `^[0-9]+$` and normalize it to a base-10 integer before the comparison |\n<!-- /ANCHOR:risks -->\n\n---\n\n<!-- ANCHOR:questions -->\n## 7. OPEN QUESTIONS\n\n- Does `--min-percent` also apply under `--file`? Decision: yes - it compares against that file's reported completion, so the gate behaves the same in both modes.\n- Is N inclusive? Decision: yes - a completion equal to N passes, matching the request's \"below N\".\n- Does the option change stderr? Decision: no - stderr is unchanged, so existing warning consumers keep working.\n<!-- /ANCHOR:questions -->\n\n---\n","_meta":{"cognition.ai/linesAdded":1,"cognition.ai/linesRemoved":0}}],"locations":[{"path":"/private/tmp/claude-501/-Users-michelkerkmeester-MEGA-Development-Code-Environment-Public/fcd93cd7-b3f2-45e6-b976-87fabe792df3/scratchpad/speed-loop/w8a66e200e3/tree/specs/zz-bench-authoring/001-completeness-min-percent/spec.md"}],"rawInput":{"file_path":"/private/tmp/claude-501/-Users-michelkerkmeester-MEGA-Development-Code-Environment-Public/fcd93cd7-b3f2-45e6-b976-87fabe792df3/scratchpad/speed-loop/w8a66e200e3/tree/specs/zz-bench-authoring/001-completeness-min-percent/spec.md"},"_meta":{"cognition.ai/inferenceToolName":"edit"}}
{"toolCallId":"call_e4bab12363c24bafa3307eb6f74f2ac0","title":"Ran bash, echo","kind":"execute","content":[{"type":"content","content":{"type":"resource","resource":{"mimeType":"text/x-shellscript","text":"bash .skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/spec/validate.sh specs/zz-bench-authoring/001-completeness-min-percent --strict; echo \"EXIT_STATUS=$?\"","uri":"tool://preview"},"_meta":{"cognition.ai/preview_is_shell_command":true}}}],"rawInput":{"command":"bash .skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/spec/validate.sh specs/zz-bench-authoring/001-completeness-min-percent --strict; echo \"EXIT_STATUS=$?\"","workdir":"/private/tmp/claude-501/-Users-michelkerkmeester-MEGA-Development-Code-Environment-Public/fcd93cd7-b3f2-45e6-b976-87fabe792df3/scratchpad/speed-loop/w8a66e200e3/tree"},"_meta":{"cognition.ai/commandNames":["bash","echo"],"cognition.ai/inferenceToolName":"exec"}}
